                "event": "Rip Current Statement",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Upton NY",
                "headline": "Rip Current Statement issued September 25 at 5:27AM EDT until September 26 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Upton NY",
                "description": "* WHAT...For the High Surf Advisory, large breaking waves of 5\nto 12 feet in the surf zone. For the High Rip Current Risk,\ndangerous rip currents. For the Coastal Flood Warning, one to\ntwo feet of inundation above ground level expected in\nvulnerable areas near the waterfront and shoreline.\n\n* WHERE...Kings (Brooklyn) and Southern Queens Counties.\n\n* WHEN...For the High Surf Advisory, until 8 PM EDT Saturday.\nFor the High Rip Current Risk, through Saturday evening. For\nthe Coastal Flood Warning, from 6 PM this evening to 6 PM EDT\nSunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Widespread flooding of vulnerable areas near the\nwaterfront and shoreline, including roads, parking lots, parks,\nlawns, and homes and businesses with basements near the\nwaterfront. Numerous road closures are likely, and vehicles\nparked in vulnerable areas near the waterfront will likely\nbecome flooded. Flooding will also extend inland from the\nwaterfront along tidal rivers and bays.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Flooding will occur over multiple high tide\ncycles tonight through Sunday. The worst flooding is expected\nwith the Saturday morning high tide cycle.",
                "instruction": "Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone property. If\ntravel is required, do not drive around barricades or through\nwater of unknown depth.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
